ar0234-rpi-dkms (0.1.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Convert format, crop and blanking to V4L2 subdev state model.
    TRY state is seeded on open and reports real mode geometry rather
    than zeros.
  * Report package version through module version field, so modinfo
    and dkms status agree.
  * Build overlay in a temporary directory during DKMS post install,
    leaving no stray build tree behind.
  * Add device-tree-compiler dependency since post install builds
    overlay with dtc.
  * d/rules: Name both remedies in version drift error.

 -- Danius Kalvaitis <danius@kurokesu.com>  Tue, 01 Sep 2026 22:55:33 +0300

ar0234-rpi-dkms (0.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Move 1080p crop 60 pixel offset from left to top.
  * Correct active area origin to 8, matching X_ADDR.
  * Report raw colorspace instead of sRGB.
  * Handle read-only HBLANK control, no longer logged as unhandled.
  * Return on pixel clock configuration failure.

 -- Danius Kalvaitis <danius@kurokesu.com>  Fri, 28 Aug 2026 16:19:32 +0300

ar0234-rpi-dkms (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release as a DKMS source package.
  * Driver state at this release:
    - 1920x1200 at up to 120 fps (full resolution), 960x600 at up
      to 237 fps (2x2 binning), 8-bit and 10-bit RAW output.
    - 2-lane and 4-lane MIPI CSI-2 at up to 900 Mbps per lane.
    - External trigger modes (pulsed, automatic, sync-sink) and
      flash output with programmable lead and lag delay.
    - ar0234 device tree overlay with cam0, 4lane, link-frequency,
      external-trigger, sync-sink, always-on and flash options.
    - Targeting Linux kernel 6.12 or newer.
    - Validated on Raspberry Pi 4 and 5, Raspberry Pi OS Bookworm
      and Trixie.

 -- Danius Kalvaitis <danius@kurokesu.com>  Thu, 02 Jul 2026 21:52:00 +0300
